  "memo": "R03 holds: the card's issuing country differs from the IP country and AVS failed. Card is the sole adverse family; no other rule condition holds, and no household exception is needed. No earlier outcome settles this order. The underlying decision-table row is §6.6(b), but the failed id_check now decides under §5.3(b): decline is standard, and escalation is prohibited because Linkage is absent. Established device and card use support a legitimate-customer alternative but do not override the failed check. The order is unshipped; decline would void and refund it and block the account. No further check is needed. This recommendation is advisory and sets no queue priority."
